%T A309245 1952785824219551870,15,18,14,4580728614212333152148,503259461,2,926,
%U A309245 10,109,36,10,436,832836278711,13,20,2451448196948930,7037029,36,33
%N A309245 Least number k > 0 which is not a divisor of n such that k^2 + n is a nonsquare powerful number (A102834).
%C A309245 De Koninck et al. gave the smallest known values for n <= 50; twelve of them, for n = 7, 11, 18, 19, 20, 23, 25, 28, 31, 32, 44 and 47, are not minimal. [Corrected by _Alper Ferudun_, Oct 16 2026]
%C A309245 McDaniel and Vanden Eynden proved that a(n) exists for all n > 0. - _Lingling Tong_, Jun 04 2026
%H A309245 Amiram Eldar, <a href="/A309245/b309245.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 1..50</a> (corrected and confirmed except for a(17), a(21), and a(37) by Alper Ferudun)
%H A309245 Charles Vanden Eynden, <a href="https://fq.math.ca/Scanned/24-4/vandeneynden.pdf">Differences between squares and powerful numbers</a>, The Fibonacci Quarterly, Vol. 24, No. 4 (1986), pp. 347-348.
%H A309245 Jean-Marie De Koninck, Nicolas Doyon, Florian Luca, and Michoacán Morelia, <a href="https://cs.uwaterloo.ca/journals/JIS/VOL14/DeKoninck/dek.html">Powerful values of quadratic polynomials</a>, Journal of Integer Sequences, Vol. 14, No. 3 (2011), Article 11.3.3.
%H A309245 Wayne L. McDaniel, <a href="https://www.fq.math.ca/Scanned/20-1/mcdaniel.pdf">Representations of every integer as the difference of powerful numbers</a>, The Fibonacci Quarterly, Vol. 20, No. 1 (1982), pp. 85-87.
%e A309245 a(1) = 682 since 682^2 + 1 = 465125 = 5^3 * 61^2 is a nonsquare powerful number and is the smallest k > 0 such that k^2 + 1 is a nonsquare powerful number.
%t A309245 powerfulQ[n_] := Min@FactorInteger[n][[All, 2]] > 1; powerfulNonsquare[n_] := !IntegerQ[Sqrt[n]] && powerfulQ[n]; a[n_] := Module[{k=1}, While[Divisible[n, k] || !powerfulNonsquare[k^2 + n], k++]; k]; Table[a[n], {n, 1, 16}]
%o A309245 (PARI) is_a102834(n) = ispowerful(n) && !issquare(n) \\ after _Charles R Greathouse IV_ in A102834
%o A309245 a(n) = for(k=1, oo, if(n%k!=0 && is_a102834(k^2+n), return(k))) \\ _Felix Fröhlich_, Jul 19 2019
%Y A309245 Cf. A001694, A102834, A140746, A309246.
%K A309245 nonn
%O A309245 1,1
%A A309245 _Amiram Eldar_, Jul 18 2019
%E A309245 a(7), a(11), a(18)-a(20), a(23), a(25), a(28), a(31) and a(32) corrected by _Alper Ferudun_, Oct 15 2026
